66963.8 gpu: world lighting-control control=dynamicLighting kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=93 triangles=80239 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant, not a material key: the pixel shader replaces the lightmap-only factor with 0.62+0.38*dot(normal, lightDirection) for 93 visible materials / 80239 visible triangles; no VMT declares it, so every surface is shaded by the same guessed direction and the baked lightmap's own direct light is counted twice; off
66963.9 gpu: world lighting-control control=specular kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=93 triangles=80239 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant: one lobe (boost 0.12, exponent 32) for 93 visible materials / 80239 visible triangles; no visible material declares $phong, so the lobe is added to materials that never asked for one; off
66963.9 gpu: world lighting-control control=bump kind=pass-switch state=refused declared=25 visible=25 resolved=25 missing=0 materials=25 triangles=14443 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=METAL/METALDOOR001 resource=materials/Metal/metaldoor001_normal.vtf reason=off: the world pass has one bump sampler slot (--world-bump) and the per-material path is off too (--world-material-bump), so the 25 visible materials that name one of 17 distinct $bumpmap textures are drawn with no normal map at all
66963.9 gpu: world lighting-control control=$bumpmap2 kind=material-key state=not-declared declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=0 triangles=0 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=no material declares $bumpmap2
